The CPU images, eim-vllm-cpu and eim-vllm-zendnn, preload LLVM's OpenMP
runtime, libomp.so, taken unmodified from Red Hat UBI 10's libomp
package and licensed, as that package declares, under Apache-2.0 WITH
LLVM-exception OR NCSA. Its text is in the image at
/usr/share/licenses/erebine/libomp/. The images preload it through
/usr/local/lib64/libiomp5.so, a symbolic link to
/usr/local/lib64/libomp.so, because that is the name vLLM looks for: the
file is LLVM's runtime, not Intel's libiomp5. Neither image contains
software under Intel's End User License Agreement for Developer Tools,
and the build of each fails if it does. eim-vllm-zendnn also contains
AMD's zentorch plugin, under the Apache License 2.0, with the AMD ZenDNN
and AOCL-BLIS binaries it bundles under the same terms; it contains no
AOCC component. The other components of both images, torch and vLLM
among them, carry their own licenses.

The eem image contains no NVIDIA, AMD or Intel software; its components
carry their own licenses.

No compose file here runs the speech or Laya images; the license page
above covers them.


