WHAT THE AMD TERMS RESTRICT

AMD licenses ROCm per component, under MIT, Apache-2.0, NCSA and BSD
licenses. What those ask of you is notice rather than restraint: keep
the copyright and license text with any copy you pass on. Two ROCm
packages, ROCprof Trace Decoder and the AOCC CPU optimizations, ship in
binary form under a separate AMD license agreement instead; neither is
in the image.

The ROCm runtime also bundles its own builds of open-source system
libraries, among them libdrm, elfutils, numactl, libnl, gmp and mpfr,
several under the GNU LGPL. Their license texts are in the image at
/usr/share/licenses/erebine/rocm-sysdeps/, and the image's routing file
names the published source for each.

